# Rule 03. ARIA is static markup plus external JS

Language-agnostic. Applies to any stack and any component syntax.

## Variables

- `{appdir}` is the source root of the app (`src`, `web`, and so on).
- Primitives live in `packages/ui/src/ui`.
- Utilities live in `packages/ui/src/utils`.
- Behavior library: https://github.com/ui8kit/aria (package `@ui8kit/aria`).

## Goal

Accessibility behavior must not depend on framework state, props or effects.
Markup is static. Behavior comes from one external script that reads the
markup contract.

## Rules

1. Native HTML5 semantics first. Add ARIA only where the native element
   cannot express the role.
2. Do not use framework reactivity (state, props, effects, watchers,
   lifecycle hooks, two-way bindings) to set, toggle or sync ARIA
   attributes such as `aria-expanded`, `aria-hidden`, `aria-selected`,
   `aria-controls`, focus handling or keyboard handling.
3. ARIA attributes in components are static. They describe structure and
   naming, not live state.
4. State, focus, keyboard and open or close behavior come from
   `@ui8kit/aria`, attached to the markup through `data-ui8kit*` contract
   attributes on the host primitive. Do not invent a parallel JS API and do
   not write a second widget tree.
5. Contract attributes are produced by helpers in `packages/ui/src/utils` and by
   the dedicated aria tag (a primitive in `packages/ui/src/ui`) for ui8kit aria.
   Screens never write `data-ui8kit*` by hand.
6. Register only the patterns the app uses, in one place (a single aria
   bootstrap file under `{appdir}`). Keep the pattern list in the project
   config in sync with it.
7. The script is loaded once, as a deferred external script or an import in
   the bootstrap file, and initialised after the document is in the DOM.
   Runtimes without a client framework call the same init.
8. Names come from `Label` or `aria-label`. Text and `id` values are passed
   from the app frame or as props. They are not generated at runtime.
9. Keep the kit focus ring. Dialogs have a name, a description, an Escape
   close and focus return. One `main` per page with `id=main-content`.

## Pattern contract (minimum set)

| Pattern | Primitive | Contract |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Dialog | `Dialog` | `data-ui8kit=dialog`, open, close and overlay attributes, labelled |
| Disclosure | `Box` with `Button` | `data-ui8kit=disclosure`, trigger and content pair |
| Tooltip | `Box` with `Text` or `Inline` | `data-ui8kit=tooltip`, child with `role=tooltip` |
| Alert | `Alert` | `data-ui8kit=alert`, or `role=alert` when urgent |

Do not put `data-ui8kit=disclosure` on a native `details`. That pattern needs
a trigger and content pair, not `summary`.

The exact attribute names for each pattern are defined by the library docs
and the markup notes inside its repository. Check there before adding a new
pattern.

## Validation

A validator must fail when:

- a component sets any `aria-*` attribute from reactive state, a prop-driven
  expression, an effect or an event handler;
- a component writes `data-ui8kit*` directly instead of using the util
  helper or the aria tag;
- a pattern is used in markup but not registered in the aria bootstrap, or
  registered but unused;
- `data-ui8kit=disclosure` is placed on a native `details`;
- the app has no `main`, or more than one, or `main` lacks
  `id=main-content`;
- a dialog has no accessible name.
